    "tStartMs": 99080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "putting ads, a mobile gaming tactic, into \ntheir platform. Electronic Arts and Take 2  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104040,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interactive both make a staggering 75% of their \nmoney from what's called microtransactions.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109920,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Microsoft announcing it is cutting about 4,800 \njobs or roughly 2.1% of the company's global  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116200,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforce. The layoffs include 1,600 Xbox workers \n[music] with more expected later this year. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like every good shameless business video essaist, \nI am going to try and make what should be a pretty  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127880,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basic industry analysis into something bigger \nand more grandiose than it probably actually is,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including the standard issue commentary on \nsociety itself. So, you've been warned, I guess.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in this case, there genuinely are a few \nfactors beyond just a handful of companies making  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142920,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a long list of dumb decisions to create the worst \nof times in what should be the best of times.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148600,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So uh the logical place to start is that long list \nof dumb decisions. Video game companies have seen  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154960,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that their product involves software people coding \nand development cycles and concluded that they are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159160,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically just tech companies. They have also \nseen that they have IP storylines and fans and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164160,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have concluded that they are media companies. \nConveniently tech companies are worth lots of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168280,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money. So a lot of the businesses in this space \nwere happy to go in this direction thinking it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172960,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would translate into tech level valuations and for \na while it did. But in the end, what they actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ended up doing was combining the worst lessons \nof the tech industry with the worst lessons of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182840,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the media industry. The first was that they \noverhired in 2020 and 2021 during lockdowns,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187920,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assuming that the pandemic boom in new gamers \nwould go on forever. Examples like Epic Games  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192760,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "swelled to around 5,000 employees along the \nway. This led to the current wave of layoffs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially since layoffs are contagious in tech. \nNobody's stock gets punished for cutting staff in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202000,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same quarter that everybody else is cutting \nstaff. Industry trackers count around 45,000  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206840,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gaming jobs cut between 2022 and the middle \nof last year, 14,600 of them in 2024 alone,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213160,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the rounds have kept coming through this \nyear. The second problem with trying to emulate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tech companies was the obsession with making \nacquisitions. Microsoft, in particular, has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
