    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "games that I would play on any given year in \nrotation. Today, I play two games. And while  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would like to make an excuse like I am getting \nold and just have more responsibility these days,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the truth is I probably spend longer playing these \ngames in any given week than I did playing all of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407000,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these. Beyond the personal anecdote, this is \na documented trend across the wider industry.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unlike other media like music or movies, people \ncan commit far far more time to consuming a video  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416800,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game. And live service games and a multiplayer \nfocus can extend that time commitment to basically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infinite. The only real limitation is the number \nof hours people have in a day. And an increasing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426680,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "share of those hours are being spent on forever \ngames. Despite recent trends and understandable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431600,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "complaints, video gaming is still largely a very \ncost-effective form of entertainment. But the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limit new games are running into is not that their \ncustomers are running out of money to spend. It's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440600,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they are running out of time to spend as \nmost of their hours are already accounted for.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445440,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to Nuzu's Playtime Tracking, in 2024, \n57% of total play time was spent on games 6 or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452080,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more years old, a further 32% on games 1 to 5 \nyears old, and only 12% on games released that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458400,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year. Back in 2021, those older games were only \ntaking 39% of play time. That share has climbed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464600,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "18 points in three years. For PC, this trend \nis even more concentrated amongst older gamers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470080,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with 67% of play time going to six-year-old \ngames, even though they theoretically have a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474600,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
