  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549600,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "apps and accounts, you know how easy it is to lose \nsight of the big picture. Monarch is a private  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554360,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ad-free personal finance platform that syncs all \nyour accounts from 13,000 plus institutions into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559440,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one clean dashboard. What I like about Monarch is \nthat it does not try to make you obsess over every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564200,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transaction. It separates your fixed and flexible \nspending, shows you your progress on goals,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and lets you know when something unusual happens. \nAll in plain English. you stay aware without being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overwhelmed. My partner and I actually use the \nshared view for our monthly budget check-ins. We  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578240,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both see the same dashboard, the same goals, and \nsame recurring bills. It has cut out most of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583160,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "awkward money conversations because there are no \nsurprises. Monarch also tracks your net worth over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587920,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time and gives you clear timelines for saving and \npaying down debt, so you can see whether you are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592600,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually making progress instead of just hoping \nyou are. And because you are the customer and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596560,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the product, Monarch is completely adree \nwith bank level encryption. No data selling,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no ads in your financial dashboard. Try \nMonarch yourself. Start the free trial,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605480,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then scan the QR code on screen or use the link \nin my description for 50% off your first year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615760,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so gamers are basically barricaded inside \nthe same five games they have been playing for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620120,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a decade, which has led many studios to \nconclude that the only logical move is to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624240,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "create the next big live service game or die \ntrying. This has created a trend of massive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "games with limitless features put together by \nhuge teams with enormous budgets. The problem  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that if these games fail to break through, \nthey become extremely expensive dead weights.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This also means that even at full price, a lot \nof these titles can't make their money back on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unit sales alone. So, they are leaning more \non in-game purchases and in-game advertising.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If these never eventuate because nobody ends up \nspending that much time in the game, losses can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be devastating even with decent upfront sales. \nAnd of course, it's a lot worse without them.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sony spent eight years and a reported $200 \nmillion on developing Concord, their big hero  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663720,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shooter answer to Overwatch. It sold an estimated \n25,000 copies, and the servers were switched off 2  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669520,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weeks after launch with full refunds all around. \nWarner Brothers did the same thing with their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673960,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suicide Squad game, which missed so badly that the \ncompany disclosed a $200 million hit to earnings.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679760,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they did it again a few months later with \na hund00 million dollar writedown mostly pinned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685640,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on multiveres. Now I know it's fun to point \nand laugh, but it's going to keep happening.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690960,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of the network effect of these games, \nthe results are increasingly polarized. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are either a smash hit or a monumental failure. \nPeople want to play games with their friends,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699800,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they play the games their friends are playing. \nAnd if their friends aren't playing a given game,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they probably won't either. Hell Divers 2 are a \nMarvel rivals or even something like Among Us and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mecca Chameleon have broken through and they are \nprinting money from people who want something to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "play with their friends. But that self-reinforcing \nconcentration means everything else is running a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718240,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greater risk of becoming another Concord. But the \nproblem is now even if they do find a cash cow,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is an incentive to milk it until it \ncurdles to find the next mega development.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729080,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sony paid $3.6 $6 billion for Bungie in 2022, then \ntapped Destiny as hard as they could to fund the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "development of Marathon, and then Marathon flopped \nas well. Sony has now written down around $766  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740880,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million on that studio in a single fiscal year. \nDestiny 2 got its final content update last month,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and about half of Bungie has been laid off. Even \nthe biggest winner of them all is slowing down.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752360,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fortnite engagement has been falling since \n2025. Epic laid off over 1,000 people this year,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "saying that they were spending significantly more \nthan they were making, and we have to make major  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cuts to keep the company funded. This heavy push \ntowards live service games that dominate people's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767040,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time and drive recurring spending also means \nthat people are increasingly treating games as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a social outlet, potentially, you might even say, \nsome modern version of a third place. As such,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hot take alert, a lot of people don't really \nwant something new. They want something familiar.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782160,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Friends like to hang out in common environments, \nand especially as the average gamer gets older,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now 36 years old in America, that becomes even \nstronger. This trend of playing fewer games,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791200,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but playing them for much longer, also explains \nthe challenges that came with the subscription  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795320,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "services like Game Pass. In theory, a modest \nmonthly subscription for access to a massive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799720,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "library of games was a great deal and probably \nmore cost-effective than getting a similar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selection of content through something like Steam. \nThe problem was that people were only playing a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808800,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "small selection of games anyway. So having access \nto hundreds of titles didn't really mean much when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were only actually playing two of them. \nMicrosoft reportedly set itself an internal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "target of 77 million Game Pass subscribers by this \nyear. Again, assuming that this was just another  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "streaming service or tech offering, this wasn't \ncompletely unreasonable. In reality, it got to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828840,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "34 million. tried that 50% price hike from earlier \nto squeeze more out of the subscribers it did have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and promptly lost around 4 million of them. Now, \nof course, this is a generalization. Everybody  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spends their time differently. And if you are \npersonally someone that likes to try a new title  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843480,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every month, congratulations. You are probably \nhaving a lot more fun than everybody else.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848160,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for everybody else, there is one place left to \nactually find extra hours in people's day. Mobile.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855160,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People just spend more time on their phones \nthan sitting down at a dedicated PC or console  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do gaming. This becomes particularly true for \nthe filthy washed masses of more casual gamers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865000,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The share of direct mobile game revenue is now \nbigger than PC and console combined, $13 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "last year against 86 billion for the other two put \ntogether. Now, you probably already knew all this,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the point is that this can be a lot more \nlucrative because mobile games are generally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much simpler in design and development and \nalso have a system more naturally conducive to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "microtransactions. Often, payment can be handled \nthrough the same phone that people are playing on,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889520,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which strips out the transaction friction that \ngames on other platforms have to fight through.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893720,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, this is well documented. But if studios \nare going to choose a proper game for real gamers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there needs to be a very good commercial reason \nwhy they wouldn't spend the same resources on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903400,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building dozens of games for a much larger, more \nlucrative market. The only real justification is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908880,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chance at making the next big live services \ngame. On the other end of the development  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913160,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spectrum, it's never been easier for independent \nstudios or even individual people to create their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917920,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own game and publish it thanks to robust game \nengines in platforms like Steam or even Roblox.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this means that basic indie games are an \nincredibly crowded space with immense competition.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More than 19,000 games were released on Steam last \nyear alone, and nearly half of them got fewer than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934680,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 user reviews. To differentiate themselves, \ngame companies have felt the need to create  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significantly higher-end titles that wouldn't \nbe possible for smaller teams to put together.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944080,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has created a missing middle of games that \nare a cut above the indie selection in terms of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948240,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "features, but aren't monster AAA titles that cost \nmore than Avatar to make. Court documents filed by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953880,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Activision revealed that Black Ops Cold War cost \naround $700 million to develop before marketing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959800,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite, well, let's be honest, not really \nbeing that much different from any other COD  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "games released in the last 10 years. In the past, \nstudios could try to create a consistent roster  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of decent games. If one of them did well, that was \ngreat. If one of them flopped, that wasn't ideal,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974320,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it wasn't crippling. Today, even the biggest \nstudios are kind of going all in on the success  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their next release with very little margin of \nerror if it doesn't work out. Now, to play devil's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983960,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "advocate a bit here, betting big is not totally \nirrational when one Fortnite can pay for 20 flops.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the problem is that everybody is making \nthat same bet at the same time into the same  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993200,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fixed pool of player hours. The frustrating part \nis that when anybody actually funds the middle, it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can still work. Expedition 33 was made by a core \nteam of around 30 people for under $10 million,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004680,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sold 5 million copies in its first 6 months, and \nswept the game awards. It obviously can work,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010480,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I guess you also need to actually make a \ngood game, which capital investment alone can't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015120,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "guarantee, and even if it does, it's probably \ngoing to get ripped off anyway. So yeah,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020200,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the third big issue is clearly one that is not \nunique to gaming. If you ever see a YouTube video  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that does well, you can be pretty sure that there \nwill be 20 other videos that copy it in the coming  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "months. Because making an original YouTube video \nnormally takes a fair amount of time and effort,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if it doesn't do well, it can cause \nserious problems. Copying a video is easy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038640,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It comes with some guarantee of success. That's \nthe exact reason why I've decided to mix things up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043320,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and steal the Smoothie King's talking points and \nthumbnail for this video. Now, hopefully it goes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without saying that I am joking. I will always \nleave a link in the description below and we  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051480,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mostly discuss different things. But the point \nis this clearly happens everywhere on YouTube  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056480,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as people just naturally follow basic incentives. \nThe same is true 10 times over for video games.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any game that does well is going to be copied \nby dozens of people with tools that make basic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game design relatively simple. This is \nespecially the case with people porting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paid indie games into Roblox for free with \ninbuilt microtransactions. Last summer,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074520,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Peak, one of Steam's bestselling games of the \nmonth, got cloned on Roblox almost immediately.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The copy pulled in 6 million visits in about two \nweeks, monetized with Roblox own microtransaction  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084560,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system, while the studio that actually made the \ngame got nothing. The game developers said that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089240,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would rather you pirate their game than play \nthe microtransaction riddled Roblox slop ripoff,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094240,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is a sentence an actual game studio felt \nthe need to post in 2025. Roblox is running  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "132 million daily users and 31 billion hours of \nengagement every quarter, which the same Matthew  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105160,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ball from earlier estimates is about the same \nengagement as Steam, PlayStation, and Fortnite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109240,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combined. Now, obviously, this is bad. But the \npoint is for large studios, it further means that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they need to make games with some kind of mode \naround them to defend against obvious ripoffs.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119760,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the easiest one is to make something too \ncomplex to copy and then integrate recognizable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "IP in addition to some guarantee of players \nbeing around for consistent online multiplayer.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, it sounds bad, but it gets worse because \nthis has literally already happened before.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The last time this industry drowned itself \nin cheap copies of whatever it was selling,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137880,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was 1983 and the American home video game \nmarket fell by around 97% in 2 years. So, yeah,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not exactly going to feel bad for the big \ngaming companies. They have made plenty of their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own mistakes and have leaned into anti-consumer \npractices to compensate for their own failing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1152760,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's not been an easy time to be a game studio \neither. Now, if you want to see this whole dynamic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "play out on a wider scale, go and watch this video \nnext to unpack the uh financial reasons we keep  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162480,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on making so much junk. And don't forget to like \nand subscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
